  "body": "Refs #1448. Part of #1448.\n\nDepends on #3324 (the shared mechanism). Do not start before #3324 is merged. The `blocked` label goes when #3324 is closed.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe twelve turning kinds have no `links` and no start field. The user cannot set where the first pass starts or where the last pass leaves. The only diameters on `main` are the range ends `bottom_dia` / `top_dia` (TaperTurning), not a start pick.\n\n## Expected\n\n- A turning pick is a point in the lathe (Z, X) plane (question 1 of #3324).\n- Start: the first pass starts at the pick (Facing, ProfileRough, ProfileFinish, GrooveRough, GrooveFinish, Part, Chamfering, TaperTurning, MultiPassTurning, FormTurning, BoringTurning). For a roughing kind this sets the start Z and the start diameter of the first pass.\n- Exit: the last pass leaves at the pick.\n- Threading keeps its G76 start judge (`crates/app/src/operation/g76_start.rs`, `generate.rs:3416`). Its row says by name that the thread start law sets the start. A change there is a separate issue.\n\nSeams: the arms `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs:2606` to `:3075`.\n\n## Laws a pick must keep (refused by name, never moved)\n\n- The start is in air, outside the stock, on the approach side.\n- The stock to leave and the groove width keep their laws.\n- The move to the start does not cross the chuck or the part.\n\n## Done means\n\n- For each kind: a pin test shows the start at the pick, and a pin test shows an impossible pick refused by name. Threading shows its \"not taken\" row.\n- Undo and redo restore the previous path. MCP `edit_operation` sets the picks.\n- Every shipped turning golden without a pick is byte-identical.\n- Work it in slices, a group of kinds for each PR.\n\nSafety floor: this changes toolpaths and posted G-code.\n",
